    {
      "id": "5ec69bb2-601a-4784-b032-c931c57ff4cf",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        112,
        16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 624,
        "height": 1056,
        "content": "## Resume Intake Automation\n### How It Works\n* Email Trigger: Watches a Gmail inbox for new messages with a PDF/DOC/DOCX attachment.\n* Parseur Upload: Sends the resume to Parseur for extraction, then waits for Parseur's own webhook to fire once parsing is complete.\n* AI Fit Scoring: Once candidate details are validated, an LLM (via Groq) scores the candidate's fit for the applied position on a scale of 1–10.\n\n### Setup Checklist\n1. Gmail: Confirm the Gmail trigger's credentials and that the filter (has:attachment + pdf/doc/docx) matches how resumes actually arrive.\n\n2. Parseur: Connect Parseur credentials to both the upload node and the Parseur Trigger webhook node, and confirm the parserId matches your resume template.\n\n3. Parseur Webhook Setup (required for the workflow to trigger):\n   - In n8n, open the \"Parseur Trigger\" node → Webhook URLs → copy the Test URL (switch to Production URL once testing is complete).\n   - In Parseur, go to your mailbox → Exports → Integrations → Add an integration → Webhook. Paste the copied URL into \"Target URL\". Name it (e.g. \"N8n Test\" / \"N8n Production\").\n\n4. OriginalDocument field (required for file download to work):\n   - In Parseur, go to your mailbox → Fields → Metadata fields → tick \"OriginalDocument\".\n   - This adds a field to the webhook payload containing {name, url} for the original file — the \"Download Original Resume File\" node uses OriginalDocument.url to fetch it (NOT the app.parseur.com dashboard URL).\n   - Note: Enabling this field only applies to new/reprocessed documents. If testing with an existing sample document, reprocess it in Parseur (mailbox → Documents → select document → Reprocess) so the field appears before testing.\n\n5. Groq: Verify the Groq API credentials and that the selected model is still available on your account.\n\n### Customization\n* Fit score threshold: Add a filter after the AI Fit Score Generator to auto-flag or notify on high-scoring candidates.\n* File type: The Drive upload is hardcoded to .docx — adjust the filename expression if resumes arrive as PDFs too.\n* Empty extractions: The \"Skip - Invalid/Empty Extraction\" branch currently does nothing further — consider logging skipped resumes somewhere for review.                                                      \n\n\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
